#
# ── Format ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# One dated block per entry. Every entry MUST carry a real `Decided-by:` line
# naming the human who authorised the descope and quoting their answer:
#
#   =========================================================================
#   ## From #<issue> — <title> (recorded <YYYY-MM-DD>)
#   <merge/PR ref + one-line state>
#
#   D1. <one-line deficiency>.
#       Decided-by: <human> on <YYYY-MM-DD> — asked "<the binary you put to
#                   them>", answered "<their verbatim answer>".
#       <what is less than maximal in the SHIPPED CODE>
#       Forward path: <the real work that would close it, and where it is
#                     tracked>.
#
# No `Decided-by:` line means it is not an entry. Do the work, or ask.
#
# Nothing in this repo reads this file. Recording here does not schedule the
# work, does not track it, and does not tell anyone — so every entry must also
# be surfaced on the issue and the PR, and stated plainly in the completion
# report. Three entries for one issue means the issue was not implemented:
# stop and say so.

## 2026-07-21 — issue #1373 (GMN logic glyph-enrichment / operator symbology plane)

- Modal-EVALUATION reasoner bridge (crates/logic/src/foundation.rs evaluate_modal_formulas,
  wired into the production reasoning driver evaluate() at foundation.rs:3424) evaluates a
  modal formula whose body is a SINGLE GROUND ATOM only. A □/◇ whose body is a compound
  formula (∧/∨/¬/→) or a nested modal is a HARD FAIL (explicit foundation_err boundary, never
  a silent partial evaluation), so no wrong modal verdict is ever produced. This delivers the
  user-authorized "frontend ST + reasoner evaluation bridge" scope expansion (beyond #1373's
  glyph-plane requirement, which needs only modal SIGNS — those are delivered and gated) at a
  scoped-down body expressiveness. FORWARD PATH: recursive per-world sub-formula evaluation
  (thread the world through a compound body, mirroring the frontend standard-translation the
  A′ frontend already performs), lifting the single-atom restriction.
- The modal reasoning capability (frontend parse_formula standard-translation branch +
  evaluate_modal_formulas) is reachable-but-UNTRIGGERED on shipped content: no modal
  logic:Formula is authored in any frontend/reasoner-ingested source (module.ttl declares only
  the operator property defs; examples/ are not ingested by the logic frontend). The capability
  is exercised by unit tests over the real parse and foundation paths (gmeow-logic-compile
  754/754; gmeow-logic modal foundation tests), not by a shipped modal instance. Authoring a
  modal formula into a reasoner-ingested source is #1377's (GMN-1 parser/writer) ingestion
  scope, which #1373 explicitly lists as out of scope. FORWARD PATH: when #1377 lands the
  parser, a parsed modal record exercises this bridge end-to-end on the shipped bundle.
